,"due_on":"2025-09-15T00:00:00Z","closed_at":"2025-09-18T17:13:14Z"},"comments":23,"created_at":"2025-03-07T23:18:47Z","updated_at":"2025-07-25T21:28:38Z","closed_at":"2025-07-25T01:42:03Z","assignee":null,"author_association":"NONE","issue_field_values":[],"type":null,"active_lock_reason":null,"sub_issues_summary":{"total":0,"completed":0,"percent_completed":0},"issue_dependencies_summary":{"blocked_by":0,"total_blocked_by":0,"blocking":0,"total_blocking":0},"body":"### Tested versions\n\nDidn't happen in 4.3, started happening to me once I upgraded to 4.4.\n\n### System information\n\nMacOS 10.14.6\nAMD Radeon R9 M370X 2 GB\nIntel Iris Pro 1536 MB\n\n### Issue description\n\nThe editor will sometimes \"half-freeze\", where some things stop working, but others still do. For example, during one of these half-freezes:\n\n* The background highlight that occurs when you hover your mouse over a button stops happening.\n* Pressing the \"add child node\" button doesn't do anything.\n* I can still type in the code editor.\n* I can still expand and hide dropdown menus in the node inspector.\n* But trying to change the value of any of the properties in the inspector doesn't work.\n* Clicking and dragging on a node in the scene panel still pops up the little sprite of it to follow the mouse pointer as I drag it elsewhere.\n* But releasing it on top of another node doesn't result in the node's position changing in the tree.\n* While dragging a node around in the scene panel, the border highlight that normally appears around another node that I've moved the mouse cursor on top of it, or the horizontal line that appears when I'm between nodes, does not appear.\n\nThis sometimes solves itself if I wait a few seconds, but usually it does not. What does almost always solve it however is changing the focus to a different, non-Godot window, and then coming back to Godot. (There's only one time that didn't work.)\n\n### Steps to reproduce\n\nIt always seems to be triggered by me doing *something*. Usually me adding a child node or changing a property value on an existing node. But I haven't figured out any way to make it happen reliably.\n\nI have tested on a new clean project and it still happens there, so it's not anything specific to the larger project I'm working on.\n\n### Minimal reproduction project (MRP)\n\nN/A","closed_by":{"login":"Repiteo","id":17489292,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE3NDg5Mjky","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/17489292?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo","html_url":"https://github.com/Repiteo","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/103780/reactions","total_count":7,"+1":7,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"timeline_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/103780/timeline","performed_via_github_app":null,"state_reason":"completed","pinned_comment":null}